course: dictionary
lesson: 14602
title: Words that can hug or hurt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words around a word. They often give you clues to its meaning. In «Baby Sam waved his podgy little fingers at me», the word fingers tells you what is podgy, and little tells you they are small. Podgy must describe something small, round and soft.
explain: Podgy is informal and mostly used in the UK. People often say it fondly, like a pet name for a puppy or a baby. But it can hurt if someone says it about a person's body to their face. Always think about how the word will feel to the person who hears it.
explain: Podgy is not quite the same as fat. A podgy puppy is cute and round, and podgy hands are soft and fleshy. To check your meaning, ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Podgy» is an adjective. Its forms are podgy, podgier and podgiest.
fact: «Podgy» means a little fat, short and soft-looking.
fact: «Podgy» can also mean soft and fleshy, as in «podgy hands» or «a podgy face».
fact: «Podgy» is informal and mainly used in the UK.
fact: Said kindly, podgy is a fond word; said about someone's body to their face, it can be unkind.
exercise: «The puppy had podgy paws and a round tummy.» What does podgy mean here? | *Chubby and soft-looking | Cold and wet | Long and thin | Very fast and clever
exercise: «Baby Sam waved his podgy little fingers at me.» Find and copy one word that tells you what podgy describes. | Sam | little | *fingers | waved
exercise: Ben says podgy is fine to say about anyone. Why must you be careful when you use it? | *It can hurt someone if you say it about their body to their face | It only means happy | It means very tall and thin | It is a formal word used in law books
test: «The podgy baby giggled and clapped.» What does podgy describe? | A baby who is fast asleep | A baby who is cross | A tall, thin baby | *A small, round, soft-looking baby
test: Which meaning fits podgy in «a podgy puppy»? | Very old | Loud and noisy | *Chubby and round | Fast and clever
exam: Which fact about podgy is true? | *It is an informal adjective, mainly used in the UK | It means happy and clever | It means very tall and fast | It is a formal word used in science books
